cs — CoreSpeed CLI

Commands:
  cs login                           Sign in through the browser
    [--org <id>]                       Sign in to this org (else pick one when you have several)
  cs logout                          Remove this machine's stored session
  cs whoami                          Show the current user, org, permissions and key ceiling
  cs switch [<org-id>]               Change the active org (prompts when no id is given)
  cs token                           Print a fresh access token (JWT)
  cs keys create <name>              Create a new API key
    [--permission <slug>]…             Give it a permission you hold (repeatable; none by default)
  cs keys list                       List your API keys
  cs keys revoke <id>                Revoke an API key by ID
  cs keys rotate <id>                Rotate an API key by ID
  cs mcp-config                      Emit MCP client config JSON (5-min bearer)
  cs connectors list                 List available connectors + connection status
  cs connectors connect <id>         Open the connector's dashboard page to connect it
  cs connectors disconnect <id>      Disconnect a connector (its single account)
    [--account <alias-or-id>]          Disconnect exactly one account, by alias or id
  cs connectors accounts list        List your connected accounts across connectors
  cs connectors accounts remove <connector> <alias>
                                     Remove one account by alias
  cs connectors accounts rename <connector> <current-alias> <new-alias>
                                     Rename one account's alias
  cs remote add <slug> --url <https://…> --auth oauth|static_bearer|none [--header <name>]…
                                     Register an org remote MCP server (admin)
    [--name "Display Name"] [--client-id <id>] [--yes]
                                       secrets are prompted on stdin; oauth auto-detects
                                       DCR (no registration endpoint → --client-id)
  cs remote list                     List this org's remote MCP connectors
  cs remote show <slug>              Show one remote connector (url, auth, snapshot)
  cs remote refresh <slug>           Re-pull its tools/list snapshot (admin, 60s cooldown)
  cs remote remove <slug>            Deregister it — registration + snapshots + credential (admin)
  cs mcp search <words…>             Find tools for a task, best match first, one line each
    [--limit <n>] [--json]             default 10; --json prints the matches' full definitions
  cs mcp get <tool>                  Show one tool in full: description, input schema, a call
    [--json]                           to start from; --json prints its definition verbatim
  cs mcp call <tool> [jsonArgs]      Call a tool and print its result: structuredContent when
    [--raw]                            it has one, else its content (JSON pretty-printed);
                                       --raw prints the CallToolResult as it arrived. Exits
                                       non-zero when the tool did not do what it was asked
  cs mcp list [--json]               Every tool, one line each; --json prints their definitions
  cs drive put <file> <path>         Store a local file at a path in your Drive (a new version
    [--mime <type>] [--access org]     when the path exists); --access org shows a new path to the
                                       organization. The type comes from the file's extension
  cs drive get <path|id> [<file>|-]  Download a file to <file> (default: its own name here), or
                                       to stdout with -; a drv_* file id or dver_* version id works
  cs drive ls [<prefix>]             List a folder's files and sub-folders, one line each
    [--recursive] [--json]             --recursive: every file under it; --json: as the server said
  cs drive mv <from> <to>            Rename or move a file (out of tmp/ keeps it)
  cs drive rm <path>                 Delete a file and every version of it
  cs drive share <path> <access>     private | org | link | public; --rotate issues a new link
    [--rotate]
  cs drive usage                     Kept bytes against the plan, and what sits under tmp/
  cs usage                           Show wallet balance (available credit) and plan
  cs tie                             Tie this machine to your org: choose a folder to share,
                                       start tied (the daemon that holds the link, also at
                                       login), then check it end to end. With no session here
                                       it shows a code to enter at app.corespeed.io/tie from any
                                       device you are signed in on; nothing signs in on this
                                       machine. With an API key in the environment the key's
                                       principal (you, or an agent) owns the machine
    [--root <folder>]                  Share a shell and files in this folder (no question)
    [--share]                          Share the machine with your organization from the start
    [--slug <slug>] [--name <name>]    Name the device
    [--pair <code>]                    A code from the dashboard's "Tie a machine": no sign-in
                                       here; the machine is whoever made the code's
    [--pair-again]                     already tied: a new credential; the old one stops working
  cs tie status [--json]             This machine's device on CoreSpeed and its daemon
  cs tie pause | resume              Refuse every call to this machine / take calls again
  cs tie provider <p> on|off         Switch a provider: shell, browser, screen or mcp:<slug>
    [--root <folder>]…                 shell: on shares the folder too; off stops sharing just that one
  cs tie mcp add <slug> [--env K=V]… [--cwd <dir>] -- <command> [args…]
                                     Host a local stdio MCP server's tools on this device
  cs tie mcp remove <slug>           Stop hosting it
  cs untie                           Revoke this machine's device, delete its credential, stop tied
                                       and its start at login
    [--forget]                         only forget it here, without asking CoreSpeed
  cs --help                          Show this help

Account & org context:
  Commands act on your active org (see 'cs whoami'; change it with 'cs switch').
  'cs connectors connect' opens the dashboard in the org active there; switch
  orgs in the dashboard first to connect elsewhere. Aliases come from
  'cs connectors accounts list' or the account badges in 'cs connectors list'.
  Shared org-wide accounts can be removed only by their creator or an org admin.

Exit codes:
  0  success
  1  usage error, or the request was refused (not found, conflict, invalid input)
  3  not signed in, or the session was rejected — run 'cs login'
  4  the account cannot do this now (no active org, payment required, suspended, permission)
  5  CoreSpeed unreachable, rate-limited or answering badly — retry later
  6  the tool call waits for a human's approval and has not run — run the
     manage__approval_wait call printed on stderr, right away

Documentation: https://corespeed.io/docs/cli
